pack.description=It's time to farm a little bit of everything! Supported version is 26.0+

item.farmersdelight:book_farmersdelight.name=The Book of Farmer's Delight

farmersdelight.book.title=Farmer's Delight
farmersdelight.book.cutting_board.main=The Cutting Board is a functional block without a GUI that can hold certain blocks and items and can be processed using tools.
farmersdelight.book.stove.main=The Stove is a functional block without a GUI that provides heat for the Skillet and Cooking Pot when active, and can also smelt certain items on its own. When smelting items, it can simultaneously smelt up to 6 different items of the same or different types.
farmersdelight.book.stove.switch_title=§l§6Ignition and Extinguishing
farmersdelight.book.stove.switch=§rWhile active, the Stove can be extinguished using a shovel or water bucket. When extinguished, it can be reignited using flint and steel.
farmersdelight.book.cooking_pot.main=The Cooking Pot is a functional block with a GUI that can be used for cooking and storing food.
farmersdelight.book.cooking_pot.heat_source_title=§l§cHeat Source
farmersdelight.book.cooking_pot.heat_source=§rTo prepare food, the Cooking Pot must have a heat source below it. You can determine the presence of a heat source by observing bubbles or smoke rising above the Cooking Pot or flames in the GUI. Heat sources can be fire (including soul fire), lava, campfires (including soul campfires), lit stoves, or any block with the tag farmersdelight:heat_source.
farmersdelight.book.cooking_pot.use_title=§l§qUsage
farmersdelight.book.cooking_pot.use.1=§r● The Cooking Pot has six input slots, one display slot, one container slot, and one output slot.
farmersdelight.book.cooking_pot.use.2=§r● The Cooking Pot has a recipe display UI, accessible by opening the Cooking Pot.
farmersdelight.book.cooking_pot.use.3=§r● The Cooking Pot recipes are all shapeless recipes; once the ingredients are placed and it is heated, the food will automatically start synthesizing.
farmersdelight.book.cooking_pot.use.4=§r● Items in the display slot cannot be taken directly; you need to put a suitable container in the container slot to transfer them to the output slot before they can be taken out.
farmersdelight.book.skillet.main=The Skillet is a functional block without a GUI. Its role differs in item and block forms.
farmersdelight.book.skillet.block_title=§l§3Block State
farmersdelight.book.skillet.block=§rIn this state, the Skillet can cook food when there is a heat source below it. Right-click to place food on the Skillet, and it can hold a maximum of one set of ingredients.
farmersdelight.book.skillet.item_title=§l§2Item State
farmersdelight.book.skillet.item=§rIn this state, the Skillet has additional attack damage.
farmersdelight.book.thanks=Credits
farmersdelight.book.thanks.sponsored_list_title=§l§eSponsors
farmersdelight.book.thanks.sponsored_list=§r@炽雨 @Lis.kai
farmersdelight.book.thanks.license_title=§l§9License
farmersdelight.book.thanks.license=§rThe original Java edition Farmer's Delight is open source on GitHub and CurseForge under the MIT license. This team has legally ported Farmer's Delight while adhering to the MIT license! Special thanks to Vectorwing for creating this excellent mod.
